Overflow of the signed fixed-width integer types Signed8.T ..
Signed64.T (this fork; see
LLVM-IR-backend-docs/fixed-width-integer-types-plan.md).

At each width, every way + - * DIV, unary -, ABS, INC and DEC can
overflow, each caught as RuntimeError.E and printed with its tag
(IntegerOverflow), next to the same operation just inside the range,
which must not fail.  The 64-bit cases include products whose wrapped
value looks plausible (2^32 * 2^32 wraps to 0).  Operands are
variables, and also constants: folding gives up on an overflowing
constant expression, which then fails at run time.  INC and DEC of a
narrow SignedN by an INTEGER check the step first, so a step that
would overflow INTEGER arithmetic still reports IntegerOverflow.  VAL
and assignment to a subrange keep ValueOutOfRange.  Main.m3 was
generated by a script; every line of output should be the same with
every backend and at every optimization level.
